=====================================================================================================
General process written up for the 1.8.5-hotfix release (Jobs, add support for apptainer fakeroot).
=====================================================================================================
   Also see confluence: https://tacc-main.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CIC/pages/512491571/Tapis+Java+Hotfix+Releases
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
General Process

1 Identify github hash for the impacted service.

2 Based on the timestamp of the service hash identify github hashes  for shared code in use at that time. Note that this must include the openapi repos.

3 Create hotfix branch for each repo

4 In the hotfix branch of repo tapis-client-java, update pom files in for clients that have a specPath. For example, for apps-client/pom.xml:
    <specPath>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tapis-project/openapi-apps/1.8.5-hotfix/AppsAPI.yaml</specPath>

5 For shared code, update snapshot versions in top level pom files to match the latest for the dev branch. Do this for branches tapis-bom, tapis-client-java, tapis-shared-java
    NOTE: The version must be updated in top level pom file and pom files in sub-directories. Easiest way to do it is to use mvn versions:set. For example:
    mvn versions:set -DgenerateBackupPoms=false -DnewVersion=2.0.222

6 Make sure to enable snapshot releases (local-only). For releases after 1.8.1 this should already be done. For the 3 shared repos, do this by checking/updating the top level pom files. For example, from tapis-bom:
7 <repositories>
    <repository>
      <id>tapis-local-snapshots</id>
      <name>Local repo for snapshots</name>
      <url><https://maven03.tacc.utexas.edu/repository/maven-snapshots</url>>
      <releases>  <enabled>false</enabled> </releases>
      <snapshots> <enabled>true</enabled>  </snapshots>
    </repository>
  <repository>

8 Note that making the local snapshots look like the most recent version even though it is older code is needed for maven to properly resolve dependencies. There might be a better way.

9 Commit shared code updates to hotfix branches.

10 Should now be possible to build shared code locally using hotfix branches. Probably best to first clean out any existing mvn cached files. E.g.

11 rm -fr ~/.m2/repository/edu/utexas/tacc/tapis

12 Build shared code locally.

13 Make sure hotfix branch of impacted service still builds locally.

14 Make the hotfix updates to the service.

15 Build the service and if possible test it.

16 In the hotfix branch for the service create a special build and publish job. Copy from an existing hotfix branch and update as needed. E.g.
      tapis-jobs/jobs_hotfix_build.sh at 1.8.5-hotfix · tapis-project/tapis-jobs
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

==================================================================
Notes written up for the 1.6.0-hotfix release
==================================================================
Preparing for a hotfix after a major release, e.g. release 1.6.0
1. Create hotfix branches for all java code repositories, for example branch name 1.6.0-hotfix
   - tapis-bom
   - tapis-client-java
   - tapis-shared-java
   - openapi-systems
   - openapi-files
   - openapi-apps
   - openapi-notifications
   - tapis-security
   - tapis-systems
   - tapis-files
   - tapis-apps
   - tapis-jobs
   - tapis-meta

2. In the hotfix branch of repo tapis-client-java, update pom files in for clients that have a specPath.
   - apps-client/pom.xml
   - files-client/pom.xml
   - notifications-client/pom.xml
   - systems-client/pom.xml

  Change specPath to point at hotfix branches. For example, for apps-client/pom.xml:
    <specPath>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tapis-project/openapi-apps/1.6.0-hotfix/AppsAPI.yaml</specPath>

Creating a hotfix deployment:
1. Check out hotfix branches for shared code: tapis-bom, tapis-client-java, tapis-shared-java.
2. Build shared code locally.
3. Check out the hotfix branch for the service that requires a change.
4. Make changes to the hotfix branch for the service. Commit updates.
5. Build the service locally.
6. Edit and run the special script to create the new docker images.
   - For example, for jobs hotfix branch 1.6.0-hotfix the script is tapis-jobs/jobs_manual_build_deploy.sh
   - The script is based on the jenkins job TapisJava -> 3_ManualBuildDeploy -> jobs
   - To run this script, the docker user and password must be set, e.g.
     - export DCKR_USER=scblack, export DCKR_PW=*********
   - The docker user must have permission to push to the appropriate docker hub repo, e.g. tapis/jobsapi
   - The script creates new docker images and tags them
     - DCKR_TAG1="staging"
     - DCKR_TAG2="prod"
     - DCKR_TAG3="1.6.0"
     - DCKR_TAG4="latest"
   NOTE: The tags above may include "staging". To build images for "prod" only, edit the script to
         comment out all references to DCKR_TAG1.